To get a Chalk instance whose colour level follows stderr instead of stdout, you can create a new instance with the `stderrColor` option set to `true` [C3:241-259]. This will configure the Chalk instance to use the color support detected for the `stderr` stream instead of the `stdout` stream [C3:241-259]. Here's how you can do it:

```js
import { Chalk } from 'chalk';

const customChalk = new Chalk({ stderrColor: true });
```

This will create a new Chalk instance that uses the color support detected for the `stderr` stream, allowing you to customize the color level according to your needs [C3:241-259].
